# Anti AI Slop

Slop is what a model produces when it averages over its training data. Test: could this
page, section, or sentence ship on a different site by changing one noun? Then it is slop.

## Process (mandatory for any UI work)

1. Use the **Impeccable** skill (`/impeccable`). Run `/impeccable init` once to write
   `PRODUCT.md` and `/impeccable document` to write `DESIGN.md`; both are the design brief.
2. Before any UI edit, read `.claude/skills/impeccable/reference/craft-floor.md`.
3. After edits: `pnpm design:detect` (source) and
   `pnpm design:detect:live` with `pnpm dev` running (catches contrast and tiny text).
4. Look at the rendered page at mobile and desktop widths before calling it done.
5. Before shipping a surface: `/impeccable critique` then `/impeccable polish`.

## Visual slop (reject)

- Default faces chosen by reflex: Inter, Roboto, Geist, Arial, Space Grotesk, Plus Jakarta Sans
- Purple/blue/violet gradients, gradient text, glow blobs, glassmorphism by default
- Centered hero + three identical feature cards + CTA band — the template layout
- Everything in rounded cards with the same shadow; uniform spacing with no rhythm
- Emoji or generic line icons as decoration; stock "diverse team smiling" imagery
- Fade-up-on-scroll applied to every element; motion without a purpose
- Gray text on colored backgrounds; contrast below WCAG AA

## Copy slop (reject)

- Buzzwords: empower, seamless, leverage, innovative, cutting-edge, revolutionary, unlock,
  holistic, ecosystem, journey, game-changing, powerful, elevate, transform, delve
- "Welcome to…", "Discover…", "Your one-stop…", "Whether you're X or Y…"
- Triads of adjectives, rhetorical questions as headings, exactly-five lists of equal shape
- Placeholder text (Lorem ipsum, "Your Name", fake testimonials, invented numbers or clients)

Write like a working professional describing their own work to a peer: flat, specific,
concrete nouns (real places, real work, real numbers the client supplied). Never invent
facts, clients, quotes, or metrics — ask for them.

## Code slop (reject)

- Comments that restate the code; "// Helper function to…"
- Defensive branches for impossible states; wrappers around a single call
- Unused props/variants "for flexibility"; copy-pasted near-duplicate components

## Exceptions

The brief wins: a pinned font, palette, or style from the client overrides a detector
warning. Record it: `npx impeccable ignores add-value <rule> <value> --reason "<why>"`.
